# Security headers for Cloudflare Pages (Phase 5).
# Cloudflare Pages applies this file to every response for the site.
# The Content-Security-Policy keeps 'unsafe-inline' for scripts and styles
# because Astro inlines the island loader script and component styles at
# build time; removing it would break calculator hydration. No external
# script, font, image, or frame source is allowed, and there is no
# third-party analytics or advertising script on the site.
#
# See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §11.
#
# /404 (Phase 13): Cloudflare Pages serves the custom 404.html file at
# the /404 path and returns HTTP 200 for it (its "pretty URL" behaviour:
# every .html file is served at its extensionless path). There is no
# Pages setting to change the status code, and a nonexistent URL still
# correctly returns 404. The /404 path is not in the sitemap and is not
# internally linked, so the risk is low — but this noindex header makes
# sure the page can never be indexed even if a crawler discovers it.
# See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §15.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'

/404
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
